  "notes": "Not encoded: angles of geometric visibility (Annex 2 tables; they depend on the lamp side and mounting height; their minimum is kept as parameter Igeo_min), the uniformity rule of Annex 3 para. 1.2, the option to check the distribution only down to 5°D for mounting heights up to 750 mm (Annex 3, 1.1), and the CoP tables 12 and 13. A lamp marked \"D\" has the lower maximum Imax_D = 600 cd (parameter only; the file checks the single-lamp maximum). SOURCE CHECK NEEDED: Table 8 prints the single-lamp maximum for this category as 1.20∙10^2 cd, which is below its minimum (400 cd), while category 11 prints 1.20∙10^3 cd. The value is copied exactly as printed. The minimum is printed as \"4,00∙10^2\" (comma as decimal mark) and read as 400 cd."
